								<div class="title" id="post-title-2239666">
																		While I agree you raised important points, this is what I think on the subject:
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doc-sanford" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1875589); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1875589&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349765" alt="Doc_Sanford" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1875589)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/doc-sanford" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1875589); return false;" >Doc_Sanford</a></span> <span class="odate time_1424855636 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Feb 2015 09:13</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2239666">
									

<p>- The AI studied nothing but things created by humans. It went through the Foundation files, all created by humans for the singular purpose of other humans. It had to go through several Dialect Upgrades just so he could fully understand it. He became more human for two purposes: For the sake of being able to analyze data as well as everyone else (Nevermind the fact he can do it FASTER- His limited dialect meant that he couldn't analyze it further) and for the sake of being able to create his own data to analyze (In order to get more data to analyze).</p>
<p>- After creating the persona, the AI allowed it to basically take over his being- Dr. Bright is not a face the AI lifts when he wants to look human- The AI IS Doctor Bright at this point. His feelings, at this point are the result of pure logic- A person would show happiness when his projects succeed, and a person would show fear when his hiding place is discovered. It may not be actualy feeling, but, in fact, his persona is such an integral part of his being that logic dictates he should at least act like he's feelign anything, even when he's not in public.</p>
<p>- The AI didn't go idle because, while he's probably AWARE he can go idle, he won't do it because he never did it. Since the moment he was created, he was never idle- He was always active, at least partially, researching and looking. Let's say, basically, that he's someone who doesn't require sleep. He knows he CAN sleep, but he probably WON'T sleep, because the concept of sleep is alien to him- he can learn about the entire biological concept of sleeping, but it wouldn't mean anything to him. The reason he starts going insane is also a result of his built-in logic- Every normal human being would react like this if they're basically locked up in a box with nothing to do for a long while. Once he created his impression of a human being, he basically stuck to it until the end.</p>

							</div>

								
					
